      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The force needed to loosen a bolt varies inversely with the length of the handle of the wrench used. This means that the product of the force and the handle length is a constant value. Let's call this constant value k.\n\nWe can write the equation as:\n\nForce * Handle Length = k\n\nWe are given that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force to loosen the bolt. We can use this information to find the value of k:\n\n375 * 9 = k\n3375 = k\n\nNow we need to find the handle length of the wrench that will require 15 inches of force to loosen the same bolt. We can use the equation we found for k:\n\nForce * Handle Length = k\n15 * x = 3375\n\nWe can solve for x, the handle length, by dividing both sides of the equation by 15:\n\nx = 3375 / 15\nx = 225\n\nSo, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require 225 pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
