      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to use the concept of inverse variation. In an inverse variation, the product of two variables is constant. Here, the force \\(F\\) required to loosen the bolt varies inversely with the length \\(L\\) of the handle of the wrench. This relationship can be expressed as:\n\n\\[ F \\cdot L = k \\]\n\nwhere \\(k\\) is a constant.\n\nFirst, we need to determine the constant \\(k\\) using the given values. We know that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force. So, we can substitute \\(F = 375\\) and \\(L = 9\\) into the equation to find \\(k\\):\n\n\\[ 375 \\cdot 9 = k \\]\n\n\\[ k = 3375 \\]\n\nNow that we have the constant \\(k\\), we can use it to find the force required for a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches. We substitute \\(L = 15\\) and \\(k = 3375\\) into the equation:\n\n\\[ F \\cdot 15 = 3375 \\]\n\nTo find \\(F\\), we solve for \\(F\\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 15:\n\n\\[ F = \\frac{3375}{15} \\]\n\n\\[ F = 225 \\]\n\nTherefore, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require \\(\\boxed{225}\\) pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
